# Milestone: M3
# Covers: a host-registered finalizable type runs its destroy callback when
#         the last reference is dropped and the GC collects the cell.
#
# blocked: T39 chk-runner host-driver (## host: / ## expect-host-call:) not implemented
# matrix-row: gc-finalizer
#
# Reason: two prerequisites are both missing at M3:
#   (1) T39 adds the ## host: / ## expect-host-call: directive support to the
#       chk runner (tests/integration/run_chk.sh).  Without it, the runner
#       cannot inject a host-registered type nor assert callback counts.
#   (2) M4 delivers the host-binding API surface (urbi_register_type with
#       TYPE_HAS_FINALIZER) and the FileHandle example binding used here.
#
# The equivalent finalizer path is unit-tested at M3 via
# tests/unit/test_ugc_finalizer.c using urbi_register_type + urbi_gc_alloc
# directly (no chk runner needed).
#
# When T39 + M4 land, activate this fixture by implementing the ## host:
# directive and uncommenting the urbiscript source below.
# Expected behaviour: the destroy callback is invoked exactly once after
# f = nil and a GC cycle runs.
#
# Fixture source (activate at T39 + M4):
#   ## host: register-finhandle-type-and-count
#   var f = FileHandle.new("/dev/null");
#   f = nil;
#   ## expect-host-call: file_handle_destroy 1
